scripts/demo-part-a-sync.sh
== 1. Same account sent 4 times to the ERP and synced 4 times
ERP POST #1 -> 201
ERP POST #2 -> 200
ERP POST #3 -> 200
ERP POST #4 -> 200
sync #1 -> 200
sync #2 -> 200
sync #3 -> 200
sync #4 -> 200
{"external_reference":"GL-13155937","status":"SYNCED","attempts":1,"last_error":null,"next_attempt_at":null}
ERP accounts: 1 | Fineract GL accounts: 1 | mappings: 1

== 2. Four concurrent sync requests for a new account
responses: 200200200200
{"external_reference":"GL-5155937","status":"SYNCED","attempts":1,"last_error":null,"next_attempt_at":null}
ERP accounts: 1 | Fineract GL accounts: 1 | mappings: 1

== 3. Fineract is down: SYNC_PENDING, retried with backoff, then SYNCED
fineract: stopped
sync -> 202
{"external_reference":"GL-2155937","status":"SYNC_PENDING","attempts":1,"last_error":"ConnectError: [Errno -2] Name or service not known","next_attempt_at":"2026-10-30T13:59:42.817339Z"}
-- after the first backoff, still down
{"external_reference":"GL-2155937","status":"SYNC_PENDING","attempts":2,"last_error":"ConnectError: [Errno -2] Name or service not known","next_attempt_at":"2026-10-30T13:59:49.217641Z"}
-- fineract restarting
fineract: healthy
-- retry loop synced it without any new request
{"external_reference":"GL-2155937","status":"SYNCED","attempts":5,"last_error":null,"next_attempt_at":null}
ERP accounts: 1 | Fineract GL accounts: 1 | mappings: 1

== 4. Fineract rejects the account (same external_id, different payload): FAILED, no retry
sync -> 422
{"external_reference":"GL-3155937","status":"FAILED","attempts":1,"last_error":"Fineract rejected the account (409): General Ledger Account with external id GL-3155937 already exists (id 17) with a different payload","next_attempt_at":null}

